course: dictionary
lesson: 4642
title: Hire: paying to use, or giving a job
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Hire has two main meanings. To hire something means to pay to use it for a while, like hiring a bike for an afternoon. In the USA people usually say «rent» instead.
explain: To hire a person means to give them a job and pay them. «A company hires new workers» when it needs more people to help.
explain: Look at the words around hire to find its meaning. Money paid for time points to paying to use something. Jobs and workers point to giving someone work.
fact: Hire can be a verb (to hire) or a noun (a hire, or bike hire).
fact: «Bike hire» means a service where you pay to rent bikes.
fact: «For hire» on a taxi means the taxi is free to take passengers.
fact: «Hire out» means to let someone use something in return for payment.
fact: When a company hires someone, it gives them a job and pays them for their work.
exercise: Dad says, «We can hire two bikes for the afternoon.» What does hire mean here? | *To pay to use something for a time | To give someone a job | To lend them for free | To buy them forever
exercise: «The company will hire ten new workers next month.» What does hire mean? | To rent a bike | To sign up to a school | *To give people jobs and pay them | To buy the company
exercise: A sign at the park says «Bike hire». What does it mean? | A bike race | Bikes that have been stolen | *Renting bikes for a time | Bikes made of wood
test: Which phrase means a taxi is free to take passengers? | Car hire | Hiring | *For hire | Hire out
test: In the USA, which word do people usually use instead of hire when they pay to use a bike? | *Rent | Steal | Buy | Borrow
exam: Which sentence uses hire to mean giving someone a job? | «The taxi is for hire.» | «The park offers bike hire.» | «We will hire a canoe for the lake.» | *«The shop will hire a new assistant on Monday.»
